## Auditor Agents (Review Role)

Specialized review agents for comprehensive audits. All auditors are **read-only** - they report issues but never modify code.

| Agent | When to Use | Focus Area | Checklist |
|-------|-------------|------------|-----------|
| `dev-auditor-performance` | Pre-deploy, after major features | N+1 queries, bundle size, renders, caching | `performance-review.md` |
| `dev-auditor-accessibility` | UI changes, pre-launch | WCAG 2.1 AA, keyboard nav, screen readers | `accessibility-review.md` |
| `dev-auditor-architecture` | Major refactors, new modules | Layer violations, coupling, boundaries | `architecture-review.md` |
| `dev-auditor-testing` | Coverage review, test quality | Gaps, flaky tests, edge cases | - |
| `dev-auditor-api` | New endpoints, API changes | REST conventions, consistency, status codes | `api-review.md` |
| `dev-auditor-docs` | Pre-release, onboarding review | README, API docs, code comments | - |
| `dev-auditor-dependencies` | Monthly, pre-deploy | CVEs, licenses, outdated, bloat | - |
| `dev-auditor-errors` | Post-incident, error UX review | Boundaries, messages, logging | - |
| `dev-auditor-responsive` | UI changes, pre-deploy | Mobile-first, breakpoints, touch targets | `responsive-review.md` |

### When to Use Auditors

**Pre-deployment review:**
```
dev-auditor-dependencies → dev-auditor-security → dev-auditor-performance
```

**Accessibility sprint:**
```
dev-auditor-accessibility → [fix issues with dev-frontend] → dev-auditor-accessibility (verify)
```

**Architecture health check:**
```
dev-auditor-architecture → dev-auditor-testing → [create remediation plan]
```

**API quality review:**
```
dev-auditor-api → dev-auditor-docs → [update documentation]
```

## SDLC Phase Mapping

```
APP DESIGN       →  UI DESIGN        →  DESIGN+CONTRACT   →  IMPLEMENT         →  VERIFY     →  REVIEW          →  AUDIT           →  DEPLOY
dev-designer        dev-ui-designer     dev-architect        dev-backend          dev-test      dev-reviewer       dev-auditor-*      dev-deploy
                                        dev-api              dev-frontend                       dev-security                          dev-docs
                                        dev-migration        dev-integration                    dev-refactor
                                                             dev-data
```

**Phase descriptions:**
- **APP DESIGN:** Feature discovery, page inventory, user flows (what to build)
- **UI DESIGN:** Visual design tokens, responsive strategy, component specs (how it looks)
- **DESIGN+CONTRACT:** Technical architecture, executable TypeScript interfaces + Zod schemas, database schema (how it works)
- **IMPLEMENT:** Implementation + co-generated unit tests (dev-backend, dev-frontend)
- **VERIFY:** Integration/E2E tests post-implementation (dev-test)

**Note:** APP DESIGN phase (using `/app-design`) should run at the start of new projects or major features. Follow with UI DESIGN (`dev-ui-designer`) for visual specifications before implementation.

## CDD Workflow

The **main orchestrator** spawns agents in sequence (agents cannot spawn other agents):

### Feature Development

```
1. dev-api      → Define contracts (TypeScript interfaces + Zod schemas)
2. tsc --noEmit → Verify contracts compile
3. dev-backend  → Implement + co-generate unit tests
   dev-frontend
4. dev-test     → Integration/E2E tests (post-implementation)
5. dev-refactor → Improve structure (REFACTOR)
6. dev-reviewer → Review quality
7. dev-analyst  → Review plan vs results (optional)
8. Commit
```

### Bug Fix

```
1. dev-test     → Write reproducer test (must fail, proving the bug)
2. dev-backend  → Fix the bug (minimum code to pass test)
   dev-frontend
3. dev-test     → Verify fix + no regressions
4. Commit
```

## Agent Selection Quick Reference

**Building a feature?**
1. `dev-api` → Define contracts (TypeScript interfaces + Zod schemas)
2. `dev-migration` → Create database schema
3. `tsc --noEmit` → Verify contracts compile
4. `dev-backend` / `dev-frontend` → Implement + co-generate unit tests
5. `dev-test` → Integration/E2E tests
6. `dev-reviewer` → Review before merge

**Fixing a bug?**
1. `dev-test` → Write reproducer test (must fail)
2. `dev-backend` / `dev-frontend` → Fix the bug
3. `dev-test` → Verify fix + no regressions

**Integrating external API?**
1. `dev-integration` → OAuth, API client
2. `dev-data` → Sync/transform data
3. `dev-test` → Integration tests

**Performance issue?**
1. `dev-database` → Query optimization
2. `dev-refactor` → Code structure

**Pre-deployment?**
1. `dev-security` → Security audit
2. `dev-reviewer` → Final review
3. `dev-deploy` → Deployment config

**Comprehensive review?**
1. `dev-auditor-dependencies` → Security/license issues
2. `dev-auditor-performance` → Performance bottlenecks
3. `dev-auditor-architecture` → Structural issues
4. `dev-auditor-testing` → Test coverage gaps
5. `dev-reviewer` → General code quality

